## Summary

Reader Lab bake-off kit K2 (Bead blog-0044.28): an owner-only compare page, so the client can choose between the five directions on the same real content.

- **Route:** `/owner/reader-lab/compare`. The owner page guard runs before any data read. The page is private, no-store and noindex: the existing `/owner/:path*` header rule applies, and the page also sets noindex metadata. It is read-only, and the only write is the existing lab-view cookie.
- **Choose a page:** home, a section, a story, an author or a topic. You can pick from a list built from published content, or enter a path. Paths must match `/`, or `/(stories|sections|authors|topics)/<slug>` with the storage slug rules; nothing else is accepted (no query, fragment, encoding tricks or owner paths). Only published content is shown; drafts and missing pages get a clear message.
- **Panels:** the registry drives the list, so every registered direction (Baseline plus the five) renders the same loaded view, with no per-direction code. Each panel is a labelled, scriptless, same-origin `srcdoc` frame at a 390 px or 1440 px preset. React portals render into the frames, so each direction's fonts and styles load only in its own frame and the parent page loads none. The global CSP (`frame-ancestors 'none'`) is unchanged.
- **Open in Reader Lab:** a per-direction button sets the existing lab cookie through the lab's own cookie policy and opens the exact page full-screen. It checks the same origin first, then the owner session (an expired session goes to sign-in), and only then reads.

New files only; no existing file changed. No migrations, packages or CI changes. Nothing links to the page yet: the Reader Lab page belongs to K4's write set, so the link is a follow-up.

## Verification (host)

- `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm format:check`, `git diff --check`: clean
- Vitest: 81 files, 853/853 (the compare suites have 25 tests: owner guard, headers and noindex, registry enumeration with a synthetic extra direction, published-only, path rejection including encoded, uppercase, backslash, trailing-slash and repeated values, cookie writes, frame font isolation, fragment links)
- Production build: clean, route `ƒ /owner/reader-lab/compare`
- Browser (Chromium, local lab, production build):
  - anonymous requests get a 307 to sign-in with `private, no-store`, noindex and a same-origin referrer;
  - signed in, all six frames render the same story with one h1 each and no broken images;
  - each frame loads only its own direction's fonts, and the parent loads none;
  - the 390 and 1440 presets set the frame viewport;
  - seven hostile or invalid paths were refused;
  - the Swiss Index handoff opened `/sections/architecture` in that direction with the lab bar;
  - a signed-out handoff went to sign-in;
  - axe (WCAG 2.2 AA plus best practice) found 0 violations at 390 and 1440 px;
  - keyboard order is header, picker, path form, scroll region, then each panel's button and frame;
  - there is no page-level horizontal scroll.
- `pnpm test:browser` (Playwright, production build, Desktop and Pixel 7 Chromium): 58/58

## Review

Implemented by the Codex worker. Cross-vendor review by Claude: PASS, with no security, correctness or data-integrity defect. It confirmed the guard order, path validation, no open redirect, no XSS route through `srcdoc` (constant document, frames with no scripts), only one cookie write, and font isolation through the portals.

The coordinator then made two changes in `e8cf944`:
1. Screen-reader labels in the scrolling panel list were positioned against the page and made it scroll sideways. The scroll region is now their containing block.
2. The full-page action now checks origin and session before any read, matching the other lab actions. More path edge cases are tested.

Known nits, left as is:
- the Next link prefetch inside frames;
- the generic error page on a stale handoff.
